From f3bc4b5705c1b5db49f522f79730208976a00f21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:26:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] charts: fill left to right again while the history is still
 short

Field report: the Sysinfo temperature graph and the QoS Diagnostics live trends
"load right to left" - they should build from the left.

Both are v2.4.6 regressions from the same change (53608bc095), and neither is an
inverted axis: newest is on the right and oldest on the left in both, correctly.
What changed is the FILL direction. Placing x by time means the window is
anchored to "now" at the right edge, so the very first sample is drawn AT the
right edge and the trace extends leftward as history accumulates. The
index-based code this replaced started at x=0 and grew rightward, because a
half-full ring simply had fewer indices. Same end state once the window fills;
completely different first minute, which is all a user watching it load sees.

Fix in both: scale x to the history actually held until a full window has
elapsed, so the oldest sample sits at x=0 and the newest advances rightward,
reaching the right edge exactly as the window fills. From that point on the
expressions are identical to v2.4.6 and the window slides as before.

  Reaper_QoSDiag.asp  state.t0 records the first sample of a run (and is
                      cleared with the rings when the object selector changes).
                      liveFrame() derives a separate x-axis edge tx = t0+span
                      while t1-t0 < span, else t1, and passes it to drawOcc /
                      drawDrops for xAt() only. t1 is deliberately left alone so
                      the drop-scale easing and its shrink-hold keep running on
                      real time - moving those onto a synthetic edge would stall
                      the y-scale for the first window.

  Tools_Sysinfo.asp   temp_points() scales to min(TEMP_SPAN_S, span held)
                      instead of pinning the newest sample to TEMP_SPAN_S. One
                      extra local and one changed expression; the axis, ticks,
                      series arrays and dataset guards are untouched, keeping
                      the stock-code change minimal and revertable.

Verified by simulation of both mappings across a full fill cycle, 16/16: first
sample at the left edge, oldest pinned at 0 while filling, newest advancing
rightward in proportion to elapsed/span, strictly increasing x, and on a full
window newest exactly at the right edge with behaviour identical to v2.4.6.
Both pages still parse under node --check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_QoSDiag.asp | 30 +++++++++++++++++------
 release/src/router/www/Tools_Sysinfo.asp  | 10 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_QoSDiag.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_QoSDiag.asp
